The legal texts come from the Laws of Malaysia portal of the Attorney General's Chambers of Malaysia
(https://lom.agc.gov.my), retrieved 29 October 2026: the English reprints of the Federal Constitution
(Reprint as at 15 October 2020 and Reprint as at 30 November 2025).

The portal's terms say: "Copyright 2023 by Attorney General's Chambers, Malaysia, all rights reserved." Federal
legislation "can be accessed and downloaded at no charge from this portal". The online reprints "are not the
reprinted version made pursuant to Section 14 of the Revision of Laws Act 1968 [Act 1]", and a print-out from the
portal "is NOT A COPY of the Gazette printed by the Government Printer for the purposes of section 61 of the
Interpretation Acts 1948 and 1967 [Act 388]". Authoritative printed copies of the Federal Government Gazette are
available from Percetakan Nasional Malaysia Berhad.

This repository is private. The texts are reproduced with the attribution above; no licence to redistribute them is
stated by the source.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; running heads, footnotes and the reprints' NOTES were left out; for
Article 119 before 15 December 2021 the words the 2020 Reprint's footnotes give as the text then in force were
read; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the Acts that made each change. The wording of the
law was not otherwise changed. The Attorney General's Chambers of Malaysia does not endorse this repository.
